From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0500: vrs: per-draw variable rate shading (RSSetShadingRate, Tier 1 semantics) chosen per render phase, a run-time load valve

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (stream LOCK60 A4). Validated in game: run lk-vrs1 (levels cycled within the run, screenshots)
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: D3D12. Cvars (GPU/VRS): vrs_level (0 = off: no shading rate ever recorded), vrs_levels (the level table, group=rate lists),
  vrs_min_target_width (640: narrower targets stay 1x1). The title's governor overrides the level through rexgpu_vrs_level (-1 =
  not governed); rexgpu_vrs_levels publishes how many levels exist (0 = unsupported, or the ROV path). 1x1 is forced for depth
  export, float24 depth conversion in the PS / sample-rate shading, narrow targets, the UI, lead/tail/swap and every internal
  draw (EDRAM transfers, clears, HDR restore); MSAA clamps to 2x2.
Bucket: REDO

0500-vrs.patch (mcla-x86 LOCK60). Measured on the 880M at 1080p (lk-vrs1): post+composite 2x2 -0.36..-0.43 ms, + translucent +
pre -0.56..-0.73 ms frame, no visible change (parked screenshot diff at the base-to-base noise level); the main scene at 2x1/2x2 was
SLOWER (+0.2..+0.5 ms) and visibly blurred, so 0510 drops those levels from the default table.

---
